        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "f89157b6-4002-5c62-a5dc-b7ddf43a3d8c",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: James B. Donovan, Francis Gary Powers, Rudolf Abel, Vilyam \"Willie\" Genrikhovich Fisher\n- Works: Bridge of Spies\n- Events: Cold War, 1960 U-2 incident, prisoner exchange\n- Organizations: U.S. Air Force, Soviet Union, United States, KGB\n\nFacts:\n- Rudolf Abel, whose real name was Vilyam \"Willie\" Genrikhovich Fisher, was born on July 11, 1903, and was a Soviet intelligence officer.\n- In 1960, Francis Gary Powers was a U.S. Air Force pilot whose U-2 spy plane was shot down over the Soviet Union.\n- Rudolf Abel was a convicted Soviet KGB spy held by the United States, and James B. Donovan represented him at trial.\n- During the Cold War, James B. Donovan was entrusted with negotiating the release of Francis Gary Powers in exchange for Rudolf Abel.\n- Rudolf Abel died on November 15, 1971.\n- The film Bridge of Spies is set during the Cold War and tells the story of James B. Donovan's negotiation involving Francis Gary Powers and Rudolf Abel.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "1069973f-b7f6-5a70-acca-7b0d0f9575c3",
        "text": "Page: Bridge of Spies (film). Sentence: Set during the Cold War, the film tells the story of lawyer James B. Donovan, who is entrusted with negotiating the release of Francis Gary Powers—a U.S. Air Force pilot whose U-2 spy plane was shot down over the Soviet Union in 1960—in exchange for Rudolf Abel, a convicted Soviet KGB spy held under the custody of the United States, whom he represented at trial.\nPage: Rudolf Abel. Sentence: Rudolf Ivanovich Abel (Russian: Рудольф Иванович Абель ), real name Vilyam \"Willie\" Genrikhovich Fisher (Вильям \"Вилли\" Генрихович Фишер), (July 11, 1903 – November 15, 1971) was a Soviet intelligence officer.",
